comments[7]:
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T16:39:33.335Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: Reviewing the assigned PR 181 findings against native behavior and the pinned oracle. Regression tests and gate results will be linked here.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T16:52:22.441Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD93 - Retained oracle parity. The 2026.11.18 lifecycle/claim.js stale branch emits Re-run with --takeover-stale. stale_foreign_claim_refusal_matches_published compares both rendered encodings exactly. Native takeover support remains tracked here.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T16:52:28.631Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD-B - Retained oracle parity. The pinned resolveItemOwnershipActivity returns its initial judgment before workspaceRestoredSince when stale_policy.stale is false. The differential now measures the 71-hour case alongside the past-threshold restore.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T17:13:15.542Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD9n - 34d1ea82c7af. Force advice now requires the corresponding policy and an unforced request. A held cleanup gate tests ordinary contention with automatic recovery.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T17:13:41.677Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs65CD_E - 34d1ea82c7af. Stage session bytes then check the lease generation and expiry under the reclamation gate before publication. A paused native writer cannot replace the attribution of a successor native writer. Mixed-runtime reclamation remains untested.
    edited_at: "2026-11-21T20:32:17.494Z"
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T17:19:31.013Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: Added a separate contention regression for a busy gate at publication. It checks the original session bytes and the removal of staged temporary data.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T18:09:20.275Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: The native concurrent-writer and unreclaimed-expiry regressions passed. The separate busy publication gate case in 9c1150b preserved the earlier bytes and removed temporary output. Mixed-runtime suspension inside the publication gate was not tested.
